        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>​​Game genre:</strong> Visual novel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>​​Clear time​:</strong> Approximately 55 minutes.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The story is fictional.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Synopsis</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  They say stories are fundamental tools for understanding the world. Yet crafting a good story demands both skill and resources. Does this inevitably mean some people possess an inherent advantage—or disadvantage—in telling their tale?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >  In the early 2020s, as the great tide of the era receded, grains of sand were settling into position. Yet young hearts forever yearn to charge forward—even when the enemy remains unseen, or when only imagined foes can be found.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3743910/extras/0febb092f1d58b367a1d1a809597109e.avif?t=1753836539\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3743910/extras_big/0febb092f1d58b367a1d1a809597109e.avif?t=1753836539 width=800 height=114 /></span></p>",
